{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head e76ca4a8215f3d0ef0d8132fdb7851271427a730 (tree 9900e9b26f783e9f6e2d3b8eb5cc638a9bb66c66), the final BO1-W1 note on published c9038871. The verdict binds the BO1-W1 implementation promise and signs the one path artifact, notes/implementation/2026-11-22-bo1-w1-commons-plan.md (1f7647e5). It carries my approval 80c009bb of the plan at 4a0b3454 forward, with the three planner corrections of act 1d6ff17a now in the note. It authorizes no provisioning, deploy or register change.\n\n## The delta\nOne commit, \"Record Commons timing and rate decisions\", changes the one note (`git diff 4a0b3454 e76ca4a8`; `git diff --name-only da69aa9f e76ca4a8` lists the same path). It touches no source, test, config or provider action.\n\n## The three corrections against planner act 1d6ff17a\n1. **Decided and open items.** The note's opening now says ruling 9b0585ca decides the Worker, cohort, matching register pair, private custody, Start removal and non-destructive rollback, and ruling e53e0500 authorizes the timed checks. The \"Decisions and missing evidence\" section now names only what stays open: the exact W1 content, the agent's role and access, the operator for each invocation, the Wrangler pin at deployment and the measured DO rate. That is the planner's list, and the section no longer reads stale after landing.\n2. **Idle baseline before Hugh.** After founding and before Hugh begins, the planner reads a baseline with `scripts/do-rate.mjs --worker dap-commons` (the `--worker` flag exists). The note prefers one complete 15-minute window at no more than 25 requests, and stops before Hugh begins if the baseline exceeds it. 25 in 15 minutes equals 100 an hour, so the scaling is exact, and the 15-minute window sits inside the 10-to-15-minute interval the planner set. A shorter window would need a lower cap, which the note does not offer.\n3. **Archive estimate.** One added sentence says none of the seven pinned cohort definitions appears